# RootForge OS — Debian security archive
# Victorious Framework | Origin Source Labs
#
# [Certain] this live-build version (3.0~a57) hardcodes the pre-bullseye
# security-suite path ("${DISTRIBUTION}/updates") for LB_MODE=debian,
# non-derivative builds — read directly from lb_chroot_archives, both the
# chroot-build-time "install" stage and the final-image "remove" stage
# that writes the persisted /etc/apt/sources.list. Debian renamed the
# security suite to "${DISTRIBUTION}-security" back in bullseye (11);
# security.debian.org/deb.debian.org 404s on the old path for bookworm
# and every release since, which is what actually caused every "exit 126"
# ISO build failure this whole session, once the recursion bug in
# auto/build (see that file's own header) stopped masking it entirely.
#
# auto/config sets --security false to suppress live-build's broken
# built-in security line (in BOTH the chroot-install and final-image
# stages) and this file replaces it via live-build's own supported
# config/archives/*.list mechanism instead — a bare ".list" (no .chroot
# or .binary suffix) applies to both the build-time chroot AND the
# persisted /etc/apt/sources.list.d shipped in the installed system, so
# one file covers both without duplicating it. Same trusted
# debian-archive-keyring already present from bootstrap covers this
# archive too, so no companion .key file is needed.
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian-security bookworm-security main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
